Title: Architecting Intelligent Microservices: Bridging the Gap Between AI and DevOps.

In DevOps, we often climb a linear ladder: master Docker, then tackle Kubernetes and eventually — perhaps — touch production-grade tooling. For a long time, I studied these in isolation, but a persistent gap remained between spinning up a container and managing a resilient, real-world system. I understood Terraform, but hadn’t yet embraced the power of modularity, I viewed ArgoCD and the Prometheus-Grafana stack as ‘end-game’ technologies reserved for the experts.

That perspective shifted when I stopped seeing these tools as isolated steps and started seeing them as a unified ecosystem. I want to give a huge shout-out to Vishakha Sadhwani, for her DevOps + AIOps Project Series. Inspired by the series, I realized that true engineering happens at the intersection of these layers. This article documents the journey of bridging those gaps — moving beyond basic containerization to build a full-scale, automated and AI-enabled microservices environment.

