https://miro.medium.com/v2/resize:fit:1100/format:webp/1*aq7dAQwN7_tJ6JLU_GxmwQ.png

Most people interact with AWS through the console. It works, until you need to recreate it, explain it to a teammate or tear it down and rebuild without missing a step. Terraform makes the cloud auditable.

The entire AWS infrastructure was provisioned through three Terraform modules, applied with a single terraform apply. The Networking module handled the VPC, subnets across 3 availability zones the Internet Gateway and route tables — the invisible plumbing that makes the cluster reachable. The EKS module provisioned the cluster itself: nodes, IAM roles and OIDC configuration for secure pod-level identity.

